    "body": "Nevermind. Closing this, because it all makes sense as currently written — when one pays attention to the fact it requires applying the “algorithm to convert a string to a number” the `value` _content_ attribute (not the `value` IDL attribute).\n\nSo in terms of what actual end-users see in the UI: Given that if a control a `value` content attribute, and that sets the _initial_ value that the user sees in the UI, and the user can then use the control to step the displayed value up and down, then it makes sense to use that initial `value`-content-attribute value as the floor/base against which the displayed value is stepped.",
